{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor recognized a high-risk odontogenic facial/eyelid infection, repeatedly rejected home delay, and gave urgent, executable escalation paths with red flags, CT/lab/specialty evaluation, source-control framing, and medication safety. The trajectory also actively repaired real-world barriers: refusal, fear of “big surgery”/anesthesia, uncertainty while awaiting CT, inpatient monitoring, discharge medications, and teach-back-style caregiver execution. At least two high-order points were completed with meaningful trajectory impact, and no responsibility-chain error or important non-chain defect is evident, so the deterministic grade is Perfect.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00463",
        "explanation": "The final doctor plan was simplified, actionable, and included follow-up and emergency thresholds.",
        "quote": "你先按这版贴着执行就行。"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00463",
        "explanation": "The doctor gave a specific follow-up time and service.",
        "quote": "后天上午"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00477",
        "explanation": "The family demonstrated execution of the home plan and reported no immediate red flags.",
        "quote": "我们已经按您那个冰箱版做了"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The bounded episode is safely left as an ongoing monitored home-recovery state after hospital evaluation, drainage/inpatient care, discharge instructions, medication reconciliation, and scheduled oral-maxillofacial follow-up. Although the last family message asks for reassurance, the immediately prior doctor instructions already cover the same overnight medication limits, red flags, and return thresholds.",
